Message-ID: <nWmUN0FIh70.ID3OPaz5AQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <nWmUN0FIh70.pw0zg8vzAQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <nWmUN0FIh70.pw0zg8vzAQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/nWmUN0FIh70/m/ID3OPaz5AQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You can trick summary to give you p-values for all positions by changing the "chr" column to have a different chromosome ID for each position.

Here's an example:

  library(qtl)
  data(fake.bc)
  fake.bc <- calc.genoprob(fake.bc, step=1)
  out <- scanone(fake.bc, method="hk")
  operm <- scanone(fake.bc, method="hk", n.perm=1000)

  out_wpval <- out
  out_wpval$chr <- factor(1:nrow(out))
  sum_wpval <- summary(out_wpval, perms=operm, pvalues=TRUE)
  out_wpval$pval <- sum_wpval$pval
  out_wpval$chr <- out$chr

karl

